## DEC-003 · `include_operations` whitelist only listed one tool

**Symptom**: `main.py` mounted the treaty sub-app with
`include_operations=["treaty_management_mcp"]`. FastApiMCP only exposes tools whose
`operation_id` appears in that list. The four other treaty endpoints
(`list_treaties`, `get_treaty_terms`, `list_exclusions`, `get_clause`) were
invisible to the agent with no error, warning, or log line.

**Measurement**: Calling `GET /api/v1/treaty/mcp` returned a tools manifest with
exactly one entry. The Treaty Agent would only be able to call `get_treaty`.

**Change**: Added all five operation_ids to the whitelist in `main.py`.

**Result**: All five treaty tools appear in the MCP manifest. This is the canonical
silent failure mode for FastApiMCP — a missing operation_id is invisible until you
inspect the manifest. Interview story: "The agent passed eval on happy-path but
couldn't list treaties or fetch clauses. No error anywhere — I had to read the MCP
spec to realise the whitelist was the gating mechanism."

